               <p xml:id="idm255">Christian Jürgensen Thomsen (1788-1865) was a historian and antiquarian. From 1816 he was head of  the collections which later developed into the National Museum of Denmark. He died on 21 May 1865. As there was only very little time, Gade, who was the organist of Holmens Kirke, and J.P.E. Hartmann divided the music between them.</p>
            </history>
